course: dictionary
lesson: 2475
title: Dawn: a time, a beginning, a moment of understanding
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dawn is a word with more than one meaning. Most often it is the time in the early morning when light first appears in the sky, just before the sun rises. «Lions hunt mostly from dusk to dawn» tells you that dawn is the time at the end of the night, when the sky starts to get light again.
explain: Dawn can also be a verb. To dawn means to begin to get light: «The sky began to dawn over the hills.» Ask yourself: is dawn a time you can point to, or is it something that happens? Context tells you which.
explain: Dawn can also mean the beginning of something big, as in the dawn of time. In the phrase «It dawned on me», dawn has nothing to do with the sky. It means I suddenly understood or realised. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Dawn is the time in the early morning when light first appears, just before the sun rises.
fact: «Dawn» can also mean the beginning of something, such as the dawn of time.
fact: To dawn means to begin to get light, and «It dawned on me» means I suddenly understood.
fact: Dawn and dusk happen because the Earth spins.
fact: «Male songbirds such as blackbirds sing at dawn» to claim territory and be noticed.
exercise: «The fog-basking beetle stands head-down on a dune at dawn.» What does dawn mean here? | A thick fog that covers the desert | The end of a long journey | *The time in the early morning when light first appears | A loud song sung by birds
exercise: Ben says, «It dawned on me that the test was tomorrow.» What does dawned mean? | I felt very sleepy | *I suddenly understood | Light began to appear | The sun rose early
exercise: «Lions hunt mostly from dusk to dawn.» Find and copy the word for the time when the night ends and light returns. | *dawn | lions | dusk | hunt
test: «The sky began to dawn over the hills.» In this sentence, what does dawn mean? | *To begin to get light | To sing a happy song | To climb a steep hill | To go to bed for the night
test: «The dawn of time» is about the very start of everything. What does dawn mean here? | A bright and sunny day | A small bird that sings | The end of a long night | *The beginning of something
exam: «Every night, huge crowds of fish swim up to feed near the surface and sink back down at dawn.» What does dawn most likely mean in this sentence? | The middle of the night, when it is darkest | *The time when light returns and the sky starts to lighten | The deepest part of the sea | A special kind of fish
